The heap window: every low_4gb mapping lies in one window at a base aligned to 4 GiB (ADR-0033 decision 3).

ART keeps a reference to an object as its address in 32 bits and asks MemMap for its heap with low_4gb, which
on arm64 scans [64 KiB, 4 GiB). iOS maps nothing below 4 GiB. At its first low_4gb request, MemMap now reserves a
window of 4 GiB without access at a base aligned to 4 GiB, so that the low 32 bits of an address in it are its
offset. Every low_4gb mapping takes a range of the window: at the address it asks for, where that lies in the
window and is free, else in the first gap that holds it, as mmap treats a hint. The window's first page stays
without access for good, so no object has the offset 0, which is null. What MemMap unmaps in the window goes back
to the reservation.

